{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1356016-artificial-novas","id":1356016,"title":"Artificial Novas.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-20T00:49:41-08:00","id":1356016,"title":"Artificial Novas.","content":"In the background for Aberrant, it's mentioned that after the Hammersmith event, the Doyen put dampers up that kept any other event from having anything more than a local effect--but that Divis Mal and his allies eventually figured out how to break that limitation. But what about previous attempts? Given how important novas are, someone, somewhere is going to give a mega-int 5 attempt at creation a device that can make a nova, especially since it's been done before. <br /> <br /> Equally, what about pre-N-Day novas. we know that Ceastus Pax was one, but should they start out as powerful, or far less powerful than N-day+ novas?<br /> <br /> Also, what sorts of undocumented features would you include? I'm thinking at the very least, a good chance of either picking up transcendence and flux or being far more vulnerable to it, explaining why Divis left that particular device in unit #212 of the Handy U-Store complex just outside of Tampa.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T04:15:21-08:00","id":1356037,"title":"","content":"I've been assuming novas before N-Day weren't as powerful, but that they got a significant boost when N-Day happened. It might not be canonical, but it let me set up some cool plots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T06:43:11-08:00","id":1356080,"title":"","content":"In a certain way, Mal forced novas to exist, so they are all kind of artificial... not that Mal picked who would and who would not erupt, but they are forced to evolve faster. That would explain the way corruption works on them. In that case, artificial novas are or similar to Superiors (limited to low corruption) or far more susceptible to corruption (doubke the amount of flux gathered)<br /> <br /> Before Mal little project, the \u201cproto novas\u201d were not as powerful as Nday+ novas, and probably they were empowered in some way by the experiment. I would make proto-novas in a way similar to Superiors, maybe with some access to quantum powers on a very limited way. Once the N-day happened I would allow them to have full nova traits and exchange their superior powers for the equivalent MEdges and MAtt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T07:58:08-08:00","id":1356099,"title":"","content":"I think that between the time the Hammersmith ends (when the Doyen put up the barrier) and N-Day there are some novas around, but they're very rare and they aren't as powerful as Aberrant-era novas (maybe more like Batman or Spider-Man level).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}